    "concise_technical_rationale": "Design intent: keep V-001 and its crude input line within design pressure (CASE-01). Deviation: More Pressure in the input line and V-001 (CASE-02, CASE-03). Causes: the PV-101 loop failing closed pressurises the vessel, and a spurious trip of SDV-30010 blocks in the upstream crude line (CASE-04). Both are credible single control or valve failures that can occur during plant life. Worst credible consequence: overpressure with loss of containment of flammable material, injuries, oil spill, material damage and lost production (CASE-05). This gives Severity IV (Critical); fatalities or major escalation are not indicated, so V was not selected. Safeguards: PSV-101 A/B relief and PAHH-102 closing SDV-30010 give two diverse layers against the PV-101 cause (CASE-06), so escalation to release is judged Remote (B). Matrix IV/B gives M. Each single-step change (IV/A, IV/C, III/B, V/B) also gives M, so the ranking is robust; H would require IV/D (e.g. an unmitigated rating) or V/C. Gap: for the spurious SDV-30010 cause, the PAHH-102 action adds no protection to the upstream line, and relief coverage of that segment is not shown. Recommendations: (1) verify PSV-101 A/B set pressure, relieving capacity for the blocked-outlet case and duty/standby arrangement; (2) confirm the upstream crude line design pressure is >= maximum shut-in pressure, or add protection; (3) confirm PAHH-102 independence from the PV-101 loop and its integrity and proof testing; (4) review SDV-30010 spurious-trip reliability. Judgment aid only, not a quantitative estimate: about 2% subjective probability that this deviation causes a flammable loss of containment over the facility life, with the listed safeguards credited.",
